hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22303","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir, meaning ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah, the one washed by the angels, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham of usury which a man consumes while he knows is worse than thirty-six adulteries."
"22304","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from ibn Abi Mulaykah, from ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib, from Kab, he said: That I commit adultery thirty-three times is dearer to me than that I eat a dirham of usury, Allah knowing that I ate it when I ate it as usury."
"22305","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from a man, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib, that a man greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he had urinated, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not return it to him until he gestured with his hand to the wall, meaning that he performed tayammum."
"22306","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban al-Ansari, then al-Mazini, Mazin of Banu al-Najjar, narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I said to him: What do you think about the ablution of Abdullah ibn Umar for every prayer, whether pure or impure, what is it for? So he said: Asma bint Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir ibn al-Ghasil narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been commanded to perform ablution for every prayer, whether pure or impure, so when that became hard upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he was commanded with the siwak at every prayer and ablution was lifted from him except for ritual impurity. He said: So Abdullah saw that he had strength for that, and he used to do it until he died."
